    "faqCta": "Let’s talk",
    "faqQ1": "How do I get from Leticia to Puerto Nariño?",
    "faqA1": "Travel to Leticia, then continue along the Amazon by boat to Puerto Nariño. Amaru can coordinate river tickets and meeting arrangements when they form part of your proposal. Confirm the departure point, current timetable and connection margins before buying onward tickets. River conditions can affect the journey.",
    "faqQ2": "When should I visit?",
    "faqA2": "The river changes throughout the year. Higher water can open\n                routes through flooded forest; lower water offers different\n                walking routes and river landscapes. Tell us your dates and we\n                will explain what is possible at that time. Rain is part of the\n                experience.",
    "faqQ7": "How many days should I stay?",
    "faqA7": "For a slower visit, the Amaru team recommends around five days and four nights in Puerto Nariño. This is a planning suggestion, not a compulsory package: tell us your dates and interests so we can discuss what fits your time and the conditions of the river.",
    "faqQ8": "Which services can be arranged?",
    "faqA8": "A proposal can bring together local guiding, river transport, entrance fees and equipment, with accommodation and meals when requested. Inclusions depend on the activities and services contracted. Review exactly what is included, what is paid separately and the full price before confirming.",
    "faqQ9": "Do I need to bring specialist equipment?",
    "faqA9": "Depending on the activity, the proposal may include boots, rain capes, hammocks or torches. Ask which items, sizes and quantities are available and what you need to bring. The equipment and food for a forest night must be specified for that overnight experience.",
    "faqQ3": "Can I arrange a guide in my language?",
    "faqA3": "Let us know your preferred language when you enquire. We will\n                confirm guide or interpreter availability and any additional\n                cost before you book. The language of this website does not\n                guarantee a guide in that language.",
    "faqQ4": "What should I bring?",
    "faqA4": "Bring light, quick-drying clothes, long sleeves, walking footwear, sun and insect protection, a reusable water bottle, personal toiletries and a waterproof bag. Carry your personal documents and any regular medication. Discuss individual health needs with a healthcare professional before travelling. Ask for the packing list for the experiences you choose.",
    "faqQ10": "Night walk or overnight stay: what is the difference?",
    "faqA10": "A night walk explores the forest after dark and ends with the agreed return; it does not include sleeping in the forest. An overnight experience continues until morning and involves different walking, sleeping and preparation requirements. Choose according to your interests and comfort, and confirm the itinerary with Amaru.",
    "faqQ6": "Is kayaking a daytime activity?",
    "faqA6": "Yes. Our Kaya / kayaking experience takes place during daylight.\n                Birdwatching and the cacao tour are separate experiences and can\n                each be requested individually. Routes depend on water levels\n                and weather.",
    "faqQ11": "Should I bring cash?",
    "faqA11": "Plan enough Colombian pesos for personal expenses, extra meals, local purchases and unexpected costs. Arrange cash in Leticia before travelling and check accepted payment methods. Internet access in Puerto Nariño can be limited, so save useful contacts and travel details for offline use.",
    "faqQ5": "How do pricing and reservations work?",
    "faqA5": "Send your dates, group size and interests on WhatsApp. We will\n                discuss availability and send a personalised proposal with the\n                total price, inclusions, payment conditions and cancellation\n                terms. An enquiry is not a confirmed booking. No payment is\n                collected on this website.",
